y was\n\nThe reapply was already committed and the review had **accepted** it. My scope was the one non-blocking finding: README and the commit message claimed nested `token`/`endpoint`/`password`/`credential` keys are *preserved as data*, but the tests only asserted they're *admitted*.\n\n**I reproduced the finding before fixing it.** On a `git archive HEAD` copy of the previous revision, a mutant that admits the document then deletes every nested blacklisted-label key from the live decoded map in `validateExtensionValue` passed `go test ./... -count=1` at **exit 0**. The claim really was unpinned.\n\n**Closed it by pinning, not correcting** — preservation is genuinely guaranteed, so the claim stands and is now backed. `TestExtensionValueObjectKeysArePreservedAsData` drives the same production `loadConfigDocument` entry and asserts **byte identity** of the re-encoded extensions map instead of a nil error. `encoding/json` sorts object keys, so a dropped, renamed, **retyped** or rewritten nested key all fail — not just deletion.\n\n## Mutants (real exit codes, scratch copies, tree restored green each time)\n\n| Mutant | Exit | Failing subtests |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Delete nested keys — **previous** revision | 0 | 0 (the finding) |\n| Delete nested keys — **this** revision | 1 | 11 |\n| Re-added key blacklist (AC-required) | 1 | 18 (was 17) |\n| Re-added nested-key blacklist (AC-required) | 1 | 21 (was 10) |\n\nBoth AC-required narrowing mutants redden *more* than before — the new tests add pinning and remove none.\n\n## Gates on committed tree `29d8cee` — all exit 0\n\n`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l ./internal` (no output), `go test ./... -count=1`, `go test ./... -cover -count=1`, full `tracecheck`, scoped `tracecheck` (6.1–6.5, 17.1/17.2/17.4), `cataloggen -check`.\n\n`internal/config` coverage **93.9% → 94.4%**, baseline from an independent archive copy. **Not run:** `scalar`/`canonicaljson` fuzz targets — outside this delta.\n\n## Commit contract\n\nAmended `1a94718` rather than adding a second commit — **one** signed commit `29d8cee`, `git verify-commit` exit 0, exactly one past checkpoint `67aed0b`. Working tree clean. Only two files differ from the accepted revision: the test file, and `LOGBOOK.md` (finding recorded; its own coverage/mutant status line refreshed since it ships in this commit).\n\nEvidence attached: `BUG-260902-2faftr_preservation-evidence.md`, `BUG-260902-2faftr_gate-logs-rev2.tar.gz`.","ttft_ms":2344,"type":"result","duration_ms":474225,"uuid":"05edf4da-adde-4960-aff0-f21233616db1","ttft_stream_ms":1888,"time_to_request_ms":15,"queued_turn_count":0}
